---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<DocLayout
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`${SITE.name} is a free, private CTC to in-hand salary calculator for India, with rates checked against official sources for ${SITE.shortYearLabel}.`}
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} answers one question well:{' '}
    <strong>
      of the CTC on your offer letter, how much actually reaches your bank account each month?
    </strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Why another salary calculator</h2>
  <p>
    Most CTC calculators get the easy part right and quietly skip the parts that change the answer:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Both tax regimes, side by side.</strong> You see the new and old regime results
      together, with the difference, rather than one assumed regime.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The Labour Code 50% wage rule.</strong> Since November 2025, Basic plus DA generally
      has to be at least half of pay. When a salary structure falls short, PF and gratuity can be
      worked out on a higher wage than the payslip's Basic, and we show when that happens.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Marginal relief done properly.</strong> Tax just above Rs 12 lakh, Rs 50 lakh and
      higher thresholds is capped the way the law requires, so earning a little more never leaves
      you worse off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Professional tax by state, with the February rule.</strong> Maharashtra and Karnataka
      charge Rs 300 in February. Where we have not verified a state's slabs, we say so instead of
      guessing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we keep it accurate</h2>
  <p>
    Every statutory rate is checked against primary sources: the Income-tax Act, 2025, the Finance
    Act 2026, the Income-tax Rules 2026, EPFO and ESIC notifications, and state professional tax
    Acts. The footer shows when the rates were last verified. The calculation code is covered by
    automated tests built from hand-worked examples. The full method is on the{' '}
    <a href="/how-it-works">How it works</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Private by design</h2>
  <p>
    Calculations run in your browser. Your salary is never sent to a server. See the{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
  <p>
    Please <a href="/contact">tell us</a>. Corrections are fixed first.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
